WEBVTT

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.160
<i>Let me throw it, Karasawa.</i>

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.570
<i>Karasawa.</i>

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.000
<i>Trust my... My slider!</i>

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.700
<i>Trust my... My slider!</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.080
<i>It's coming!</i>

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.790
<i>I've been waiting for this!</i>

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.930
Batting fourth: catcher, Karasawa-kun.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.170
<i>Do your best, Shigeno.</i>

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.850
<i>Just win one more game, and it's the Kaido game that you've dreamt about!</i>

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.770
<i>The ones to go up against Kaido...</i>

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.280
<i>will be us!</i>

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.330
Shigeno!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.600
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.500
<i>The painkillers are starting to wear off...</i>

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.630
Strike!

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.170
Batter out!

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.910
Three outs! Change!

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:45.360
The two-run homer that Karasawa hit late in the game...

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.830
It's become quite a struggle... for Shigeno.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.080
It's become quite a struggle... for Shigeno.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.280
Those two runs are heavy.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.230
Strike!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.260
Batter out!

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.310
All right!

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.110
Darling struck out all three of them!

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:18.300
Yes! It's great that Shigeno-senpai's back on his feet.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.780
This should carry some momentum into our at-bats in the final inning!

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.240
Yeah!

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.710
But, this inning starts at the bottom of the order...

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.780
I-It'll be fine.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.710
Damn it!

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
<i>I shouldn't have let them hit.</i>

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.680
<i>I was counting on not letting them score any runs in order to win.</i>

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.590
<i>The pain in my leg is no excuse. </i>

00:03:54.600 --> 00:04:00.560
<i>I was preoccupied by the shock from missing Katori's slider and let them hit my strikes so easily... </i>

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.730
<i>It's all because of that.</i>

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:08.520
Top of the ninth inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.480
Batting seventh: center fielder, Takahashi-kun.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.900
Takahashi! It doesn't matter how, just get on base!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.960
Do whatever it takes! We have to break up the perfect game!

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.710
Strike!

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:27.800
Batter out!

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.710
Batting eighth: right fielder, Noguchi-kun.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:38.360
<i>You're perfect, Katori.</i>

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.610
<i>Your pitches right now are good enough to go up against Kaido.</i>

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.030
<i>In a week, the Kaido that rejected us in the last entrance exam...</i>

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.110
<i>We can finally get our revenge against them!</i>

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.330
Strike!

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.360
I-It's no good.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.240
It's not like we can suddenly expect to get a walk against this pitcher now.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.290
Strike!

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:07.840
Strike!

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.510
Batter out!

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.310
So this is where Shigeno gets eliminated...

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:20.520
Batting ninth: left fielder, Yamamato-kun.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.920
Well now.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.910
We're going back, Magura-kun.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.150
You want to leave at this point in the game?

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.310
I understand Katori and Karasawa's abilities well enough.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.910
It's not a surprise if these guys win with a perfect game.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:36.870
Well...

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:42.910
It's too bad we didn't get an opportunity to send off that idiotic brat with our own home run.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:45.740
Strike!

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.970
<i>I have to...</i>

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.470
<i>I have to do something.</i>

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.710
<i>If I get on,</i>

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.430
<i>then Shigeno-senpai will have a chance too!</i>

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.570
<i>Anyway, I need to hit it!</i>

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.480
A safety bunt?

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.250
<i>S-Seriously?</i>

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.670
All right!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.440
Katori!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.620
It's a perfect game!

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:33.650
No! No! No!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.690
It's a dead ball.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.300
The count is still 0-2.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.680
Hey, are you okay?

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.150
Doctor!

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.710
This isn't good.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.120
It might have fractured some bones.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.050
You should go to a hospital as soon as possible.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:01.790
I thought there was a weird sound...

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.540
So it hit your hand?

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.330
Yeah.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.270
Yamamoto.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:10.290
S-Sorry, I'm nothing but trouble...

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.910
Y-You're not at fault.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.250
Yeah, you just did whatever you could to get on base.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.880
Seishuu, please send in your pinch-hitter.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.680
A pinch-hitter?

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.720
Our members are...

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.690
There's no choice, is there?

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.350
Shall I become the last batter?

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:31.980
Taiga!

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:35.320
Shimizu-kun, is your hand all right?

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:39.990
Well, this injury just needs some medicine,

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.780
so I can at least hold the bat.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.120
Seishuu High School is announcing a change in players.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:52.090
Replacing the batter, Yamamoto-kun: Shimizu-kun.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.390
The last at-bat...

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.830
And it's two outs and 0-2.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.550
They must be feeling a lot of pressure from being pushed so far.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:05.970
Play!

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:13.780
<i>None of the other batters could hit his slider,</i>

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.990
<i>so some guy seeing Katori's pitches for the first time can't possibly hit them.</i>

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:19.810
<i>I'm counting on you, Taiga.</i>

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.450
<i>Let me get to the plate!</i>

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.330
<i>I'd like to let you hit it because you're cute, but...</i>

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:27.750
<i>the party ends here.</i>

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.620
<i>It's goodbye!</i>

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:34.540
Foul!

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:36.590
H-Hey...

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.710
Wasn't that the slider just now?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:39.700
Yeah.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.520
That Taiga... He cut it just like that?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.260
<i>I get it!</i>

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:50.210
<i>It's hard for a right-handed batter to go for the outside slider,</i>

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:55.240
<i>but it's still easy for a left-handed batter like Taiga to close in on it.</i>

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.330
<i>No.</i>

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.770
<i>That's, of course, just on top of his good batting sense.</i>

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:04.650
<i>I'll correct myself.</i>

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.530
<i>You're not so cute after all,</i>

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:07.500
<i>you brat!</i>

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:11.620
It got through!

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.860
All right!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.370
You did it, Taiga!

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.210
Awesome, Taiga!

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.080
We broke up the perfect game.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:19.750
All right! 

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.800
Get in, Shigeno!

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:23.470
That's the way!

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.130
Batting first: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.090
ALL RIGHT!!!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.780
Don't worry about it, Katori.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:32.200
We'll finish it off!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:37.060
Our goal is to win this game and defeat Kaido!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:41.100
Even if we didn't get the perfect game, we'll get them with just one more.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:41.100
I'm fine.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.920
Don't worry, Karasawa.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:48.860
Rather, this man being the last one to bat...

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.050
That's not bad either.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:55.710
Play!

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.460
<i>This guy...</i>

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.600
<i>What's he aiming for in an at-bat like this?</i>

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:06.790
<i>Whatever.</i>

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:11.360
<i>Even if he aims for it, he didn't even graze it his previous at-bat.</i>

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.240
<i>We'll finish him off right here!</i>

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.560
Strike!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.140
<i>I see...</i>

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.200
<i>He really did give up on the sliders since he can't hit them.</i>

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.280
<i>Simple guy.</i>

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:30.760
<i>You'll never earn the right to fight Kaido with those weak senses!</i>

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.850
It went over.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:10:59.950
No way.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.780
It's a 2-2 tie.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:18.870
This is a free fansub.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:18.870
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.200
<i>T-This can't be!</i>

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.290
<i>T-This can't be!</i>

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:28.510
<i>He shouldn't have been aiming for the slider!</i>

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:35.220
<i>No, even if he did aim for it,
he wasn't even able to graze it in the previous at-bat!</i>

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:39.450
<i>So how can he suddenly hit a home run!?</i>

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:46.410
If you could hit it, do it earlier, Senpai.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.570
As long as I hit it, you won't have any complaints, right?

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.290
W-Wait!

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.480
Were you playing us?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.110
Didn't you pretend that you couldn't hit it in the at-bat before,

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:08.870
so that you could make us pitch to you this inning?

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:10.810
Me?

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:12.480
Come on.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.980
What are you talking about?

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.580
Go back to the bench.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.680
If I were able to plan something like that,

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.520
I could've hit any ball, couldn't I?

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.780
Even if I think about it, that won't let me hit it.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:30.980
So I just calmed down and focused on hitting whatever ball came at me without thinking, that's all.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:37.550
J-Just what's this all about?

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:41.010
In the previous at-bat, he completely missed the slider.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.990
How did he hit it so easily this time?

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.370
Katsuragi.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.790
He's exactly the kind of player that catches the eye of us professional scouts.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.340
After the battery in the previous at-bats threw sliders to Shigeno for three innings,

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:57.980
seeing the same pitch over and over again,

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:01.590
and being able to respond to that subconsciously is the level of a professional ball player.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.280
Well, not just a foul or hit,

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.920
but hitting a home run...

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:11.790
He's no ordinary guy.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.730
You can tell he has good senses and concentrates well.

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:20.700
Batting second: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.780
M-My...

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.560
M-My...

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.670
My slider was hit?

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.480
Katori!

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.510
Keep yourself together!

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.000
It's still tied!

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.930
We just need to hit a walk-off homerun to win!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.920
Keep it going, Tashiro!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.310
This is our chance!

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.350
The pitcher's a wreck!

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.530
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.230
<i>You're amazing after all, Shigeno.</i>

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.600
<i>It's like he's playing this game by himself.</i>

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:53.360
<i>No, it's because we're powerless that he has to do it all by himself.</i>

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:57.680
<i>How pathetic.</i>

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:02.330
<i>Am I only useful for catching Shigeno's pitches!?</i>

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:04.760
What?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.720
Kawaguchi, get it!

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.870
H-He did it!

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:42.620
A come-from-behind home run!

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:48.330
You did it, you bastard!

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.090
Stop it!

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.760
Not yet... It's not over yet.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.910
Stand up, Katori.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:57.730
Stand up!

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:08.400
Batting third: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.850
All right, bring it!

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:14.920
Strike!

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.300
Batter out!

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:18.080
Three outs! Change!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:21.000
Am I nothing but this?

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.780
All right, it's the last one!

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.210
Do your best!

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.170
Taiga!

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:33.520
Is your hand okay?

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.610
Can you throw properly?

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:40.390
Well, it should be fine for relay throws.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.080
Besides that, what about you, Senpai?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.130
Make sure you bring them down this time.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:50.100
Your foot doesn't have the freedom to fight through extra innings, right?

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:54.720
<i>That kid...</i>

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:58.070
<i>So he noticed the pain in my foot.</i>

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.280
Batting second: left fielder, Mori-kun.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.220
<i>Bring it, Shigeno!</i>

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.740
<i>Just three more, and then Kaido's next!</i>

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.200
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.220
Strike!

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.250
Batter out!

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:22.200
<i>All right!</i>

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:23.980
<i>Just two more!</i>

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:28.340
Batting third: pitcher, Katori-kun.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.610
<i>The game's not over yet!</i>

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:44.200
Fair!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.120
All right!

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:57.380
Safe!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.800
<i>He...</i>

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.380
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:11.500
<i>I was wondering why... It was so strange with his batting senses...</i>

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:12.860
<i>That kid,</i>

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.730
<i>he has some injury, so he can't throw the ball properly.</i>

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.700
Batting fourth: catcher, Karasawa-kun.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.320
Tie it up first, Karasawa!

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.200
A sacrifice fly'll do it!

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.150
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:34.370
<i>If it goes to left field, it'll definitely be a sacrifice fly.</i>

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:36.750
<i>I'll bring them down by throwing it inside!</i>

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:41.550
<i>I knew that would come!</i>

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:45.670
Taiga!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:50.500
All right! The left fielder can't throw!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.350
It's a tie!

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.610
Out!

00:17:54.610 --> 00:18:00.380
<i>We don't have the strength to fight in extra innings.</i>

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.030
<i>Even if... my fingers tear apart...!</i>

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.550
Katori!

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.700
Slide, Katori!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.370
Out!

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.940
Game over!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.270
We did it!

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.420
We did it!

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.460
Bow!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.260
Thank you.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.050
Hey!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:21.440
Huh?

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.110
Kaido won't be like this.

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:27.430
Every single one on their team is like us, after all.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:30.650
Losing in a way I don't want to acknowledge...

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.060
Make sure you don't give us any more shame, got it?

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.410
Yeah.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:35.930
Out!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.060
Game over!

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.440
The game was called in just five innings...

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:51.500
As expected, Kaido's on a different level.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:54.990
For just the prefectural tournament, nothing else would be expected.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:00.430
We made the right choice in not inviting the others to see this.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:05.130
If they saw this game, they'd just lose all their will to play.

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.130
Tashiro.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:13.690
Sorry, but can you go back before me and practice?

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.600
I have a little business to take care of.

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:16.970
S-Sure.

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:17.740
S-Sure.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:22.060
Then I'll make up something to tell the other guys for now.

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.720
S-Senpai!

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:46.680
Senpai!

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.560
Yakushiji-kun!

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.170
There's a weird looking one with them!

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:02.290
Toshi-kun!

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.150
Toshi-kun!

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.520
Toshi-kun!

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.870
Come on, don't push!

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:11.990
You can't come any closer!

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:13.650
Toshi-kun!

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:16.660
Look only at me!

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:18.810
Yo.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:20.380
You've got yourself some nice popularity.

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:22.530
I'm quite envious.

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:26.850
For showing off your strength with that stoic face, you get these girls screaming all over you.

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.560
You again?

00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:31.250
What do you want?

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:33.300
I don't have any business with you.

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:34.840
H-Hey, you!

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:39.510
Now you can't ignore me anymore.

00:22:43.800 --> 00:22:44.930
Well, that's fine.

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:48.650
How long can you pretend to be so easy going?

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:52.020
I'll definitely stop you guys in your tracks!

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:08.360
<i>Goro-kun. </i>

00:24:40.760 --> 00:24:43.380
At last, it's the finals against Kaido!

00:24:43.380 --> 00:24:45.470
The stage is the Oceans Stadium.

00:24:45.470 --> 00:24:47.520
Are you watching, Dad?

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:51.350
All of Seishuu's members and I will take this head on and make a ruckus!

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.110
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.110 --> 00:24:55.580
The Challenge Against The King.

00:24:55.580 --> 00:24:58.120
Run to the stage of your dreams!
